Frontend: React + TypeScript + Vite, Tailwind, shadcn/ui, Axios, TanStack Query,
react-router, react-hook-form + zod, native WebSocket (NO STOMP).
Reference layout: `docs/ui/reference-draft-board.png`.
Tests: Vitest, Playwright.

Infra: Docker, Docker Compose, Nginx. NO Redis, NO Kafka, NO Celery.

Keep dependencies minimal. Ask before adding any library not listed here.

## ARCHITECTURE

Package-by-feature, layered inside each feature:

```
backend/
  pyproject.toml
  alembic.ini
  alembic/versions/
  app/
    main.py                # FastAPI app, lifespan, router registration
    config.py              # pydantic-settings
    db.py                  # engine, async session factory
    common/                # Clock, errors, base model, time utils
    auth/
    tournament/
    team/
    player/                # Player, Season, PlayerSeason
    draft/
    match/                 # Matches & Bans (replaces squad)
    importer/              # CSV import (ETL)
    <feature>/
      api.py               # routers + request/response schemas (Pydantic)
      service.py           # application/use-case layer (transactions live here)
      domain.py            # entities (SQLAlchemy models) + pure business rules
      repository.py        # DB queries
  tests/
    unit/
    integration/
```

Rules:

- Routers (api.py) only: receive request, validate input, call a service, return response.
  NO business logic in routers.
- Business rules live in service.py / domain.py. Turn-rotation logic is PURE Python
  (no FastAPI, no SQLAlchemy session, no DB) so it can be unit-tested without a database.
- SQLAlchemy models double as domain entities (do not split persistence/domain models).
- `DraftOrderStrategy` (Protocol): `LinearOrder` implemented (1..N, 1..N), `SnakeOrder` later.
- `TimeoutPolicy` (Protocol): `AutoPickCheapest` implemented as default (auto-picks cheapest valid ACTIVE cards in allowed seasons up to remaining picks in turn); `SkipTurn` alternative; `AutoPickBest` later.
- `Clock` (Protocol) with `now() -> datetime` (timezone-aware UTC). Inject it everywhere.
  NEVER call `datetime.now()` / `datetime.utcnow()` directly outside the real Clock
  implementation. Tests use a `FakeClock`. No `sleep` in tests.
- Dependency direction: api -> service -> domain; repository -> domain. `domain` must not
  import fastapi, api modules or repository modules. Enforce with import-linter in CI.
- Use FastAPI `Depends` for session, current user, clock and services.

