## DOMAIN (see design.md for full detail)

Multi-season pool model:

- `Season` (id, code, name, badgeUrl nullable, game, year, createdAt): e.g. code="23UCL", badgeUrl="/badges/23ucl.png".
- `Player` (id, name, externalPlayerId, createdAt): stable identity only. `externalPlayerId` is REQUIRED for deduplication.
- `PlayerSeason` (id, playerId, seasonId, position, rating nullable, salary INT, imageUrl nullable,
  status[ACTIVE,INACTIVE], stats nullable). UNIQUE(player_id, season_id). Stores original game position (no collapsing, e.g. LWB, RWB, CF).
- `Tournament` (id, name, status[DRAFT,READY,RUNNING,COMPLETED,CANCELLED], rules jsonb, createdAt, updatedAt).
  No season_id column (tournaments draw from multi-season pool defined in rules).
  `rules` is validated by Pydantic `TournamentRules`:
  - `rules_version`: int
  - `rosterSize`: int (1..60, default 24)
  - `budget`: int (default 305)
  - `pickTimeSeconds`: int (default 30)
  - `uniqueBy`: VARCHAR[PLAYER,CARD] (default PLAYER)
  - `timeoutPolicy`: VARCHAR[SKIP_TURN,AUTO_PICK_CHEAPEST] (default AUTO_PICK_CHEAPEST)
  - `allowedSeasonIds`: list[UUID] (empty = all seasons allowed)
  - `banCount`: int (default 5)
  - `banTimeSeconds`: int (default 60)
  - `banTarget`: VARCHAR[OPPONENT_ROSTER,OWN_ROSTER] (default OPPONENT_ROSTER)
  - `banOrder`: VARCHAR[SIMULTANEOUS,ALTERNATING] (default SIMULTANEOUS)
    Status: READY when >= 2 teams exist (or when an active draft is cancelled), RUNNING when the draft starts, COMPLETED set manually by ADMIN.
- `Team` (id, tournamentId, name, draftOrder, budgetUsed, status). N teams, never hard-code 4. A team's roster is simply its `DraftPick` rows.
- `DraftSession` (id, tournamentId, status[WAITING,PICKING,PAUSED,COMPLETED,CANCELLED],
  currentRound, currentTurn, currentTeamId, turnStartedAt, turnExpiresAt, remainingMillis,
  rulesSnapshot jsonb, version, createdAt, completedAt). Cancelled sessions are preserved in the DB as history.
- `DraftPick` (id, draftSessionId, teamId, playerSeasonId, playerId, uniqueByPlayer bool, round, turnNumber, salaryAtPick, pickedAt).
- `DraftEvent` (id, draftSessionId, type[START,PICK,SKIP,PAUSE,RESUME,COMPLETE,CANCEL], teamId,
  turnNumber, payload jsonb, createdAt). Append-only audit log.
- `Match` (id, tournamentId, homeTeamId, awayTeamId, status[SCHEDULED,BAN_PHASE,BANS_LOCKED,COMPLETED],
  scheduledAt nullable, rulesSnapshot jsonb, banStartedAt nullable, banExpiresAt nullable, homeConfirmed bool, awayConfirmed bool, version, createdAt, updatedAt).
- `MatchBan` (id, matchId, banningTeamId, targetTeamId, playerSeasonId, createdAt).
- `User` (id, username, passwordHash, role[ADMIN,TEAM_USER], teamId nullable).
- `Session` (id = random token, userId, expiresAt, createdAt) for login sessions.

Positions: stored as game's original string (ST, CF, LW, RW, CAM, CM, CDM, LM, RM, CB, LB, RB, LWB, RWB, GK). UI groups into filter chips.
IDs are UUIDs.

## DATABASE RULES

- Alembic only. NEVER `Base.metadata.create_all()` in app code except inside test fixtures
  that first run the real Alembic migrations. Prefer running real migrations in tests.
- Autogenerate is only a starting point. Review every migration by hand. Autogenerate misses
  partial indexes, CHECK constraints and some server defaults: write those explicitly.
- Set a SQLAlchemy `naming_convention` on metadata so constraint/index names are stable.
  Stable names are REQUIRED because IntegrityError handling maps constraint names to errors.
- Enums: VARCHAR + CHECK constraint (no PG enum types). Timestamps: `timestamptz`
  (`DateTime(timezone=True)`), always timezone-aware UTC in Python. Salary/budget: INT.
- Constraints:
  - `draft_picks`: UNIQUE(draft_session_id, player_season_id),
    partial unique index UNIQUE(draft_session_id, player_id) WHERE unique_by_player,
    UNIQUE(draft_session_id, turn_number)
  - `teams`: UNIQUE(tournament_id, draft_order), CHECK(budget_used >= 0)
  - `draft_sessions`: version INT NOT NULL DEFAULT 0, partial unique index UNIQUE(tournament_id)
    WHERE status IN ('WAITING','PICKING','PAUSED')
  - `seasons`: UNIQUE(code)
  - `player_seasons`: UNIQUE(player_id, season_id)
  - `players`: UNIQUE(external_player_id)
  - `matches`: version INT NOT NULL DEFAULT 0
  - `match_bans`: UNIQUE(match_id, banning_team_id, player_season_id)
- GIN index with `pg_trgm + unaccent` on `players.name` for player name search (Alembic migration must create an immutable wrapper function for unaccent because PG unaccent is not IMMUTABLE). The importer must NOT use fuzzy matching (deduplication strictly by externalPlayerId). Player list endpoints are paginated.

## PICK RULES (POST /api/drafts/{id}/picks, body: {playerSeasonId, expectedVersion})

The whole operation runs in ONE transaction (one `async with session.begin()` in the service):

1. Load DraftSession with `SELECT ... FOR UPDATE` (`with_for_update()`). All operations on a
   draft (pick, timeout, pause, resume, cancel) go through this lock.
2. Draft exists (DRAFT_NOT_FOUND); status PICKING (DRAFT_NOT_ACTIVE / DRAFT_COMPLETED).
3. expectedVersion == version, otherwise reject (stale client).
4. If now > turnExpiresAt: apply the timeout in the SAME transaction (locking the draft row,
   applying TimeoutPolicy to auto-pick or skip the turn, advancing turn,
   consuming turn, incrementing version, writing event); commit; only after leaving the
   `async with session.begin()` block raise TURN_EXPIRED (the service returns a result indicating expiry
   and the outer layer raises). Never open a second transaction on the same draft row (avoids self-deadlock).
   Broadcast the updated state after that commit.
5. Resolve the team from the authenticated user. NEVER trust a teamId from the client.
   Must equal currentTeamId (NOT_YOUR_TURN).
6. PlayerSeason exists (PLAYER_NOT_FOUND); status is ACTIVE (PLAYER_NOT_AVAILABLE);
   belongs to allowed seasons if allowedSeasonIds is non-empty (SEASON_NOT_ALLOWED);
   not already picked in this draft (PLAYER_ALREADY_PICKED).
7. budgetUsed + salary <= budget (BUDGET_EXCEEDED). budgetRemaining = budget - budgetUsed,
   computed on the backend.
8. Team roster < rosterSize (TEAM_ROSTER_FULL).
9. Budget feasibility: budgetRemaining - salary >= (slotsLeft - 1) \* minSalaryInPool
   (BUDGET_INSUFFICIENT_FOR_ROSTER).
10. Insert DraftPick (with playerId, uniqueByPlayer, round, turnNumber, salaryAtPick),
    update budgetUsed, increment version, write DraftEvent.
11. Advance turn logic: advance the turn via DraftOrderStrategy to the next team.
    After the last team, currentRound += 1 and wrap back to smallest draftOrder.
    Skip teams whose roster is full. Draft becomes COMPLETED after all rosters are full, or after
    rosterSize rounds, or if no ACTIVE unpicked PlayerSeason with salary <= any team's budgetRemaining exists.
    Write DraftEvent(COMPLETE).
12. Reset turnStartedAt / turnExpiresAt using Clock when the turn advances to a new team.
13. Commit. ONLY AFTER the commit succeeds, broadcast the new DraftState over WebSocket.
    Never broadcast inside the transaction.

- Draft start validation (POST /api/tournaments/{id}/draft/start): requires tournament status
  READY (>= 2 teams), and allowed seasons having >= teams \* rosterSize ACTIVE PlayerSeasons
  (otherwise DRAFT_POOL_TOO_SMALL, 422). Draft start resets teams.budget_used = 0 for all teams
  in the tournament and copies rules into draft_sessions.rules_snapshot.
- Catch `IntegrityError` and map it by CONSTRAINT NAME:
  draft_picks unique on player_season or player -> PLAYER_ALREADY_PICKED; on (turn_number) -> stale turn.
  Any other IntegrityError is a bug and must surface as 500.

## TIMER

- Backend is the source of truth: store turnStartedAt / turnExpiresAt for drafts, banStartedAt / banExpiresAt for matches.
- A background task started in FastAPI `lifespan` loops about once per second:
  - Finds PICKING drafts with turnExpiresAt < now, and handles each in its OWN transaction.
  - Finds BAN_PHASE matches with banExpiresAt < now, and locks bans in its OWN transaction.
    Must survive server restarts (no in-memory timers). Cancel cleanly on shutdown.
- Timeout handler for draft: lock draft row, RE-CHECK version and expiry, then apply
  TimeoutPolicy (default AutoPickCheapest: auto-picks the cheapest ACTIVE unpicked card in allowed seasons;
  SkipTurn skips the turn). Consumes turn, increments version, writes event.
- Pause stores remainingMillis, increments version. Resume sets turnExpiresAt = now + remainingMillis, increments version.
- Never block the event loop (no `time.sleep`, no sync DB calls, no heavy CPU in handlers).

## REALTIME

- Plain WebSocket endpoints sending JSON (NO STOMP):
  - `/ws/drafts/{draft_id}`: draft updates
  - `/ws/matches/{match_id}`: match ban updates
- Authenticate using session cookie at handshake. Check `Origin` against allowed list.
- Single Uvicorn worker in v1 (document in README). Periodic ping/heartbeat.
- Draft payload: full DraftState snapshot {draftId, version, serverTime, status, currentRound,
  currentTurn, currentTeamId, turnStartedAt, turnExpiresAt, rulesSnapshot,
  pickedPlayer{playerSeasonId, playerId, name, position, salary, season{id, code, badgeUrl}},
  teams[{id, name, draftOrder, budgetUsed, budgetRemaining, pickedCount}]}.
- Match payload: full MatchState snapshot {matchId, version, status, scheduledAt, banStartedAt,
  banExpiresAt, homeTeam, awayTeam, bans: (full list if BANS_LOCKED, otherwise filtered per team/spectator)}.

## MATCHES & BANS (replaces squad lock)

- Tables `matches` and `match_bans`. Created manually by ADMIN (no auto fixture generation in v1).
- Admin starts ban phase: POST /api/matches/{id}/bans/start (status -> BAN_PHASE, snapshots ban rules, sets ban timer).
- Bans:
  - Target player must belong to the target team's drafted roster (PLAYER_NOT_IN_ROSTER, 422).
  - Maximum `banCount` per team (default 5, BAN_LIMIT_REACHED, 422).
  - `banTarget`: OPPONENT_ROSTER (default) or OWN_ROSTER.
  - `banOrder`: SIMULTANEOUS (default) or ALTERNATING. In SIMULTANEOUS mode, opponents and spectators
    only see the count of bans made until both teams confirm; bans lock when both teams confirm
    (POST /api/matches/{id}/bans/confirm) or when timer expires (keeping bans made so far).
  - While BAN_PHASE: POST /api/matches/{id}/bans to add ban, DELETE /api/matches/{id}/bans/{banId} to remove ban.
  - Once a team confirms, it cannot add/delete bans (BANS_ALREADY_CONFIRMED, 422).
  - Once status is BANS_LOCKED, all bans are revealed and locked.
- Tournament status COMPLETED is set manually by ADMIN via POST /api/tournaments/{id}/complete.

## SECURITY

- Roles ADMIN / TEAM_USER. Login creates a row in `sessions`; the cookie holds only the
  random session token (HttpOnly, SameSite=Lax, Secure in production). Same-origin via
  Nginx (no CORS needed). bcrypt passwords.
- Implement dependencies `get_current_user`, `require_admin`, `get_current_team`. Every
  endpoint declares its access rule explicitly through a dependency.
- ADMIN: create tournament (with rules), add team, import players, create users (POST /api/admin/users),
  start draft (resets teams.budget_used to 0), pause/resume/cancel draft (POST /api/drafts/{id}/cancel sets tournament back to READY, keeps cancelled session as history), create matches, start ban phase, complete match, complete tournament.
- TEAM_USER: view draft, pick only on own team's turn, view roster, manage/confirm bans for own team.
- Ownership is always checked on the backend. Add tests proving a TEAM_USER cannot pick for
  another team, ban for another team, or call an admin endpoint.

## ERRORS

Define a `DomainError` base class (code, http_status, message) and register exception
handlers returning RFC 9457 style JSON:
`{"type", "title", "status", "code", "message"}`. Never return a stack trace. Unexpected
exceptions -> 500 with code INTERNAL_ERROR and a log entry with a request id.
HTTP mapping: NOT_YOUR_TURN 403, PLAYER_ALREADY_PICKED 409, \*\_NOT_FOUND 404, other business
rules 422, validation 400/422.
Codes: DRAFT_NOT_FOUND DRAFT_NOT_ACTIVE NOT_YOUR_TURN PLAYER_NOT_FOUND PLAYER_NOT_AVAILABLE
PLAYER_ALREADY_PICKED SEASON_NOT_ALLOWED BUDGET_EXCEEDED BUDGET_INSUFFICIENT_FOR_ROSTER
TEAM_ROSTER_FULL DRAFT_COMPLETED TURN_EXPIRED DRAFT_POOL_TOO_SMALL MATCH_NOT_FOUND
MATCH_NOT_ACTIVE PLAYER_NOT_IN_ROSTER BAN_LIMIT_REACHED BANS_ALREADY_CONFIRMED BANS_LOCKED
POOL_LOCKED.

