POST/GET /api/tournaments/{id}/matches (ADMIN creates match, list matches)
GET /api/matches/{id}
POST /api/matches/{id}/bans/start (ADMIN)
POST /api/matches/{id}/bans (TEAM_USER add ban)
DELETE /api/matches/{id}/bans/{banId} (TEAM_USER remove pending ban)
POST /api/matches/{id}/bans/confirm (TEAM_USER confirm bans)
POST /api/matches/{id}/complete (ADMIN)
FastAPI generates the OpenAPI spec. Generate TypeScript types from it with
`openapi-typescript` for the frontend.

## IMPORT (ETL) — keep it a clean pipeline

Source: CSV files from public datasets or FC Online exports.
CSV Columns: `external_player_id, name, season_code, position, salary, rating, image_url`
(rating and image_url optional). Unknown `season_code` automatically creates a `Season` row.
Module `app/importer/` with three clearly separated steps:

1. Extract: stream the CSV in chunks (pandas `chunksize` or `csv`), never load everything.
2. Transform: pure functions, easy to unit-test:
   - Position: original position string stored (no collapsing, e.g. LWB, RWB, CF, ST, GK).
   - Salary: read directly from CSV. `SalaryMapper` is an optional fallback only if salary is missing.
   - Row validation with Pydantic: externalPlayerId is REQUIRED; rows without it are skipped and reported.
     Salary must be an integer >= 1.
3. Load: batch upsert (`INSERT ... ON CONFLICT DO UPDATE`) into players and player_seasons.
   Idempotent: importing the same file twice must not create duplicates; re-import updates salaries and player metadata.
   Both re-import and `PATCH /api/admin/player-seasons/{id}` are rejected with `POOL_LOCKED` (422)
   if any draft session is in `PICKING` or `PAUSED` status.
   Return an import report: rows read, inserted, updated, skipped (with reasons).
   Available both as CLI (`uv run python -m app.importer --file ...`) and as admin endpoint.
   An offline standalone script `docs/tools/calibrate_salary.py` is available to generate synthetic salaries from ratings before import.

## FRONTEND

Pages: Login, Tournament list/detail, Draft board page, Match & Ban page.
Draft board page (styled per `docs/ui/reference-draft-board.png`):

- Columns per team showing draft order, budgetUsed, budgetRemaining, pickedCount, picked cards.
- Player card: season badge, season code, position, rating, salary, player name.
- Available player pool with position filter chips (FW, MF, DF, GK) and text search.
- PICK button enabled only on team's turn when valid. Realtime updates via WebSocket snapshot.

## TESTS (must exist by the end)

Unit (no DB):

- pick on turn OK; wrong turn rejected (NOT_YOUR_TURN);
- one pick per turn: turn immediately advances to next team after pick;
- inactive player rejected (PLAYER_NOT_AVAILABLE);
- season not allowed rejected (SEASON_NOT_ALLOWED);
- already picked card rejected (PLAYER_ALREADY_PICKED);
- already picked player rejected when uniqueBy=PLAYER (PLAYER_ALREADY_PICKED);
- same player allowed when uniqueBy=CARD;
- budget exceeded rejected; roster full rejected (rosterSize);
- salary update (PATCH / re-import) rejected with POOL_LOCKED when draft is PICKING or PAUSED, accepted otherwise;
- salary validation: salary must be an integer >= 1;
- timeout -> AutoPickCheapest auto-picks 1 card and advances turn; SkipTurn skips turn and advances turn;
- draft completed after all rosters full or max rounds or no affordable card;
- cancel draft sets tournament back to READY; draft start resets teams budget_used to 0;
- pause/resume recomputes expiry;
- ban player not in target team roster rejected (PLAYER_NOT_IN_ROSTER);
- ban limit exceeded rejected (BAN_LIMIT_REACHED);
- ban on already confirmed team rejected (BANS_ALREADY_CONFIRMED);
- simultaneous ban hides opponent player identity until both confirm or timer expires;
- bans locked on confirmation or timeout.

Integration (testcontainers PostgreSQL, real Alembic migrations):

- concurrent picks of the SAME PlayerSeason using `asyncio.gather`: exactly ONE succeeds;
- pick vs timeout race on the same draft;
- importer runs twice on fixture CSV -> no duplicates; auto-creates Season for unknown code;
- auth: TEAM_USER cannot act for another team or call admin endpoints;
- match ban concurrent submission and confirmation.
  Playwright: two browser contexts see realtime pick and ban updates.
  CI commands: `uv run ruff check .`, `uv run mypy --strict app`, `uv run lint-imports`, `uv run pytest`.

## CODE QUALITY

Readable, small functions, meaningful names, no dead code, no commented-out code.
Do not add features not listed here. If a requirement is ambiguous, pick the simplest
sensible option, note it in the summary, and continue.
Phase order is defined in docs/roadmap.md
